WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.373
In a blended family,

2
00:00:02.373 --> 00:00:05.241
the usual plan can backfire.

3
00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:11.100
Meet Pat, who remarried and has two kids from before.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.532
Pat leaves everything to the new spouse,

5
00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:21.100
trusting them to take care of the kids later.

6
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.872
But once it's the spouse's,

7
00:00:23.872 --> 00:00:25.862
the spouse decides.

8
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:27.105
A new will,

9
00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:28.562
a new partner,

10
00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:30.587
even a fair decision,

11
00:00:30.587 --> 00:00:34.100
and the kids may get nothing.

12
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.063
The reverse also happens.

13
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:40.435
Pat leaves everything to the kids,

14
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:44.600
and the spouse may lose the home.

15
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.701
A trust can split the roles.

16
00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.874
The spouse gets income,

17
00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:51.834
or use of the home,

18
00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.046
for life.

19
00:00:53.046 --> 00:00:58.100
After that, what remains goes to the children.

20
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.689
A neutral trustee can reduce conflict.

21
00:01:01.689 --> 00:01:03.793
Clear writing helps too,

22
00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:05.696
about who pays taxes,

23
00:01:05.696 --> 00:01:08.600
repairs, and insurance.

24
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.599
Beneficiary forms, a prenup,

25
00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:14.600
and titling matter just as much,

26
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.600
because they can override the plan.

27
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.719
Every family is different.

28
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:27.100
A short conversation can show you the options.
